WEBVTT

00:49:57.413 --> 00:50:02.079
the systems would say we've just designed
them around what humans want to do.

00:50:02.121 --> 00:50:04.538
You said, well, if someone wants
to click on something,

00:50:04.829 --> 00:50:09.329
we will give them more of that thing. And
what could possibly be wrong with that?

00:50:09.329 --> 00:50:10.871
We're just supporting human choice,

00:50:11.288 --> 00:50:16.371
ignoring the fact that humans are
complicated, farshid animals for sure,

00:50:16.413 --> 00:50:18.371
who are constantly making choices,

00:50:18.371 --> 00:50:22.663
that a more effective version of
themselves would agree is not in their

00:50:23.079 --> 00:50:25.329
long term interests. So
that's one part of it.

00:50:25.454 --> 00:50:27.788
And then you've got layered
on top of that or

00:50:27.788 --> 00:50:34.746
the complications of systemic
complexity where, you know,